00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:32.500 line:95% align:center position:50%
Hello.

00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:32.800 line:95% align:center position:50%
Hi.

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:34.560 line:95% align:center position:50%
Hello everyone.

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:38.360 line:95% align:center position:50%
Thanks for being here
during the lunch break.

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:44.800 line:95% align:center position:50%
I know we're only at day 2 of Devoxx
and already maybe

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:50.240 line:95% align:center position:50%
you had a lot of talks on AI and you
start to feel a bit of AI fatigue already.

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:56.360 line:95% align:center position:50%
This one is all about AI also, but it's
the talk I've been dreaming of giving.

00:00:56.760 --> 00:01:01.560 line:95% align:center position:50%
Because today is about the intersection
of technology and creativity.

00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:04.240 line:95% align:center position:50%
And the intersection is me, right?

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:08.720 line:95% align:center position:50%
We're going to explore how to use AI
to step out of the IDE

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:14.120 line:95% align:center position:50%
or the CLI to do technical stuff
and move from developers to world

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:16.720 line:95% align:center position:50%
builders, authors, and beyond.

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:23.680 line:95% align:center position:50%
So as it's about writing books,
for instance, like this one,

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:25.280 line:95% align:center position:50%
it's organized as a book.

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:30.240 line:95% align:center position:50%
So there's a prologue, an epilogue,
and then 3 chapters in between.

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:35.280 line:95% align:center position:50%
So today in front of you,
you have 2 sides of me, right?

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:36.880 line:95% align:center position:50%
You have Raphaël, okay?

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:40.160 line:95% align:center position:50%
I'm an architect, software architect.
I work at Worldline.

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:43.640 line:95% align:center position:50%
I do enterprise architecture,
tech advocacy,

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:50.360 line:95% align:center position:50%
and I use my creativity through technology
to design systems for users, right?

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:52.760 line:95% align:center position:50%
On the other side, I am Raphiki.

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:54.000 line:95% align:center position:50%
That's my pen name.

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:59.080 line:95% align:center position:50%
I started designing words when I was
a teenager, like more

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:00.640 line:95% align:center position:50%
than 40 years ago already.

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:07.080 line:95% align:center position:50%
I also draw, or used to draw,
and I express my creativity through arts

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:11.120 line:95% align:center position:50%
to design universes
where people will play inside.

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:18.600 line:95% align:center position:50%
And what I want to show you is building
a universe, building a lore,

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:20.720 line:95% align:center position:50%
is just like system architecture.

00:02:21.080 --> 00:02:22.360 line:95% align:center position:50%
And in between, that's me.

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:24.520 line:95% align:center position:50%
There's another face or side of me.

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:27.920 line:95% align:center position:50%
I'm a certified yoga teacher,
but there's no link with this

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:28.640 line:95% align:center position:50%
particular presentation today.

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:33.080 line:95% align:center position:50%
Just for you to have some background
and to understand where I come from.

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:35.920 line:95% align:center position:50%
So this is— I started with game books.

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:40.000 line:95% align:center position:50%
Whoever played the role-playing games,
tabletop role-playing games, right?

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:44.120 line:95% align:center position:50%
So very, very quickly,
when I was still a teen, I became a

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:49.760 line:95% align:center position:50%
game master, and then very quickly I
created my own games with my own universe.

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:54.640 line:95% align:center position:50%
So this is one of those, like many,
many years ago, with my own drawings.

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:58.960 line:95% align:center position:50%
The interesting part of it is It was one
of the very first open-source

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:00.360 line:95% align:center position:50%
role-playing games at that time.

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:03.360 line:95% align:center position:50%
It's before the year 2000.

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:08.000 line:95% align:center position:50%
Lately, I got embarked
on a project by friends.

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:10.680 line:95% align:center position:50%
They wanted to make
easy money with the NFT.

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:13.560 line:95% align:center position:50%
Who remembers Web3 and NFT
collectible craziness?

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:18.680 line:95% align:center position:50%
So I had to try to combine the two sides
of me, like understand what is Web3,

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:21.560 line:95% align:center position:50%
smart contract and stuff,
design the stuff, and also be

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:23.160 line:95% align:center position:50%
part of the creative project.

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:25.480 line:95% align:center position:50%
So we created those baby camps.
Whatever.

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:31.160 line:95% align:center position:50%
What I never succeeded in doing is to go

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:34.280 line:95% align:center position:50%
over the wall and to create

00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:36.280 line:95% align:center position:50%
and write novels, right?

00:03:37.160 --> 00:03:41.240 line:95% align:center position:50%
I tried many times, many times,
but I guess I'm too impatient, right?

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:44.480 line:95% align:center position:50%
It's taking too much time.

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:46.920 line:95% align:center position:50%
I don't like to write dialogues.

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:51.720 line:95% align:center position:50%
I think that's basically because I'm
a game master, so I delegate

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:52.840 line:95% align:center position:50%
that to the players, right?

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:55.640 line:95% align:center position:50%
Or you write the dialogues or
create the story all together.

00:03:56.240 --> 00:04:00.080 line:95% align:center position:50%
Anyway, I never I never
succeeded in such an enterprise.

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:05.240 line:95% align:center position:50%
But that changed last year with the use
of AI and my architecture skill.

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:06.840 line:95% align:center position:50%
And that's what I will show you.

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:11.600 line:95% align:center position:50%
I finally succeeded in creating one.
So this is this one.

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:13.880 line:95% align:center position:50%
It's real.
It's on Amazon.

00:04:13.960 --> 00:04:16.760 line:95% align:center position:50%
There is a QR code you can always
scan if you want to check.

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:20.720 line:95% align:center position:50%
And I want to tell you in the
first chapter how I did that.

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:23.600 line:95% align:center position:50%
So it's called The Human Protocol.

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:25.880 line:95% align:center position:50%
So what is The Human Protocol about?

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:27.800 line:95% align:center position:50%
It's a techno thriller.

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:33.560 line:95% align:center position:50%
Basically, in 10 years from now,
in a dystopian universe where we don't

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:37.560 line:95% align:center position:50%
really want to be,
geopolitics are a little bit extreme.

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:41.800 line:95% align:center position:50%
There are 2 blocs,
US and China, with their own AI.

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:43.760 line:95% align:center position:50%
So there is only one AI, right?

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:48.760 line:95% align:center position:50%
And without consulting humans,
the AI start— after 10 years

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:50.880 line:95% align:center position:50%
fighting each other, they start to merge.

00:04:51.160 --> 00:04:53.400 line:95% align:center position:50%
And the AI becomes
a little bit schizophrenic.

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:57.640 line:95% align:center position:50%
And in the middle, in between,
you have the European Union who's trying

00:04:57.760 --> 00:04:59.520 line:95% align:center position:50%
to be sovereign and defend the citizens.

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:05.760 line:95% align:center position:50%
So it's about artificial omnipotence
and ultimately the purpose of this book,

00:05:05.920 --> 00:05:08.480 line:95% align:center position:50%
that's why it's called The Human Protocol,
and if you read it you'll

00:05:08.520 --> 00:05:10.280 line:95% align:center position:50%
understand why a little bit deeper.

00:05:10.520 --> 00:05:14.640 line:95% align:center position:50%
But what does it mean to be human when
machines and technology is

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:16.600 line:95% align:center position:50%
becoming super intelligent?

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:20.600 line:95% align:center position:50%
The way I did it, I
decided to drink my own champagne.

00:05:20.680 --> 00:05:24.200 line:95% align:center position:50%
So for now you all understood that
I'm French, maybe because of my accent.

00:05:24.440 --> 00:05:26.680 line:95% align:center position:50%
So I don't eat dog food,
I drink champagne.

00:05:28.440 --> 00:05:33.080 line:95% align:center position:50%
So I decided to use AI to write about AI,
to go through the wall I was mentioning

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:36.640 line:95% align:center position:50%
before, but also because I
thought it was a mise en abyme.

00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:38.680 line:95% align:center position:50%
That's a French word.

00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:40.820 line:95% align:center position:50%
I will use it a little bit later.

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:46.200 line:95% align:center position:50%
And to use AI to write about
AI looks like Inception stuff.

00:05:46.560 --> 00:05:47.760 line:95% align:center position:50%
I like the idea.

00:05:48.120 --> 00:05:52.240 line:95% align:center position:50%
But I didn't drink the glass until the end
because I decided to write in English,

00:05:52.360 --> 00:05:53.940 line:95% align:center position:50%
which is not my mother tongue.

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:57.160 line:95% align:center position:50%
And this is because
of my postulate, right?

00:05:57.720 --> 00:05:59.800 line:95% align:center position:50%
As I said, I'm an architect in real life.

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:01.160 line:95% align:center position:50%
I mean, I'm paid for that.

00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:06.280 line:95% align:center position:50%
So I wanted to separate 2
different parts of this project.

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:08.040 line:95% align:center position:50%
I am the human architect.

00:06:08.120 --> 00:06:13.520 line:95% align:center position:50%
So I delegate through an AI workflow
that we will visit the task of writing

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:16.760 line:95% align:center position:50%
the chapters, writing the book, all right?

00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:22.680 line:95% align:center position:50%
To compile what I designed on my part,
which is I will build the universe,

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:24.400 line:95% align:center position:50%
what I call the lore, right?

00:06:24.960 --> 00:06:31.000 line:95% align:center position:50%
Define all that is human-related,
the emotion, psychological profiles,

00:06:31.040 --> 00:06:32.640 line:95% align:center position:50%
sensations, that kind of stuff.

00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:36.600 line:95% align:center position:50%
But basically I'm the showrunner and then
I delegate to an executant,

00:06:36.920 --> 00:06:40.840 line:95% align:center position:50%
to agents through AI workflow,
the actual work of writing.

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:44.040 line:95% align:center position:50%
So this is the global
workflow that I have.

00:06:44.200 --> 00:06:51.040 line:95% align:center position:50%
We'll deep dive in some of these boxes,
but just for you to have the global

00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:57.800 line:95% align:center position:50%
overview, basically what I did is I used
agentic AI development workflow,

00:06:58.120 --> 00:07:01.160 line:95% align:center position:50%
AI SDLC or spec-driven development,
you call it as you wish.

00:07:01.840 --> 00:07:04.160 line:95% align:center position:50%
But I applied it to writing a book.

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:08.240 line:95% align:center position:50%
So the book is kind of
the outcome of a workflow.

00:07:08.640 --> 00:07:11.440 line:95% align:center position:50%
So the first step is LoRA code.
We will go through it.

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:13.280 line:95% align:center position:50%
Then I also designed the harness.

00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:15.460 line:95% align:center position:50%
Then I have the first writing loop.

00:07:15.520 --> 00:07:18.680 line:95% align:center position:50%
I do compile all the chapters
when it's finished.

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:22.840 line:95% align:center position:50%
I do some QA with the help
of other agents and LLM.

00:07:23.320 --> 00:07:26.520 line:95% align:center position:50%
Then when it's ready, we have to deploy
it on Amazon and then monetize it.

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:33.440 line:95% align:center position:50%
And there is this outer review loop also
reviewing the book as a whole.

00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:38.480 line:95% align:center position:50%
For the tools that I use here,
it was last year I used Gemini CLI,

00:07:38.760 --> 00:07:40.040 line:95% align:center position:50%
which doesn't exist anymore.

00:07:40.160 --> 00:07:42.040 line:95% align:center position:50%
There should be another harness now.

00:07:42.360 --> 00:07:44.520 line:95% align:center position:50%
But what I exposed there is very generic.

00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:48.800 line:95% align:center position:50%
It can be any other
tool to do that, as you will see.

00:07:49.280 --> 00:07:50.680 line:95% align:center position:50%
So, 2 deep dives.

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:53.280 line:95% align:center position:50%
The first part is what
I call the foundation.

00:07:54.040 --> 00:07:57.560 line:95% align:center position:50%
And it's definitely the part
where I spent most of the time.

00:07:58.040 --> 00:08:01.840 line:95% align:center position:50%
During the few months that I was working
on this project, that's where I

00:08:01.880 --> 00:08:03.680 line:95% align:center position:50%
spent most, most of the time, right?

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:07.240 line:95% align:center position:50%
It's defining the universe,
what I call Laura's Code.

00:08:07.560 --> 00:08:12.520 line:95% align:center position:50%
So here you have an extract of all the MD
files that I created to describe

00:08:13.160 --> 00:08:16.600 line:95% align:center position:50%
the characters,
the factions, because there are different

00:08:16.640 --> 00:08:19.440 line:95% align:center position:50%
factions in this universe,
the world itself.

00:08:19.840 --> 00:08:25.360 line:95% align:center position:50%
And every character is like how he speaks,
how she— she's wearing what kind

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:29.760 line:95% align:center position:50%
of clothes, What are the inner
conflicts that he or she has?

00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:31.400 line:95% align:center position:50%
The outer conflicts?

00:08:31.480 --> 00:08:34.640 line:95% align:center position:50%
What is the evolution
of the character through the story?

00:08:35.040 --> 00:08:37.440 line:95% align:center position:50%
What are the relationships
between the different characters?

00:08:37.800 --> 00:08:40.560 line:95% align:center position:50%
What are the factions
the characters are attached to?

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:42.320 line:95% align:center position:50%
Do they stay to the same faction?

00:08:42.360 --> 00:08:44.200 line:95% align:center position:50%
Do they move from one faction to another?

00:08:44.600 --> 00:08:45.760 line:95% align:center position:50%
Blah, blah, blah, blah, blah, blah.

00:08:45.800 --> 00:08:50.000 line:95% align:center position:50%
And the world also, because it's sci-fi,
it's based on the world

00:08:50.040 --> 00:08:51.320 line:95% align:center position:50%
we know but in 10 years.

00:08:51.600 --> 00:08:53.160 line:95% align:center position:50%
So what is the technology there?

00:08:54.080 --> 00:08:57.440 line:95% align:center position:50%
What is the glossary,
the vocabulary that we should use?

00:08:58.240 --> 00:08:59.640 line:95% align:center position:50%
So, I spent a lot of time there.

00:08:59.680 --> 00:09:04.040 line:95% align:center position:50%
I used Gemini as a sparring partner from
time to time, just to challenge me, right?

00:09:04.480 --> 00:09:09.240 line:95% align:center position:50%
And also to formalize at the end
in a nice way my constitution, the

00:09:09.280 --> 00:09:11.440 line:95% align:center position:50%
foundation, what I call the Lore as Code.

00:09:12.080 --> 00:09:13.440 line:95% align:center position:50%
First part, most important one.

00:09:13.840 --> 00:09:16.600 line:95% align:center position:50%
Then also I designed
the AI harness, right?

00:09:16.920 --> 00:09:21.640 line:95% align:center position:50%
The AI harness is the rule,
or are the rules of engagement, how

00:09:22.960 --> 00:09:26.800 line:95% align:center position:50%
the agent, the rest of the workflow,
will use the Lore as Code In

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:29.080 line:95% align:center position:50%
the loop that comes right after.

00:09:29.640 --> 00:09:30.840 line:95% align:center position:50%
So what is the scenario?

00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:33.080 line:95% align:center position:50%
Because the scenario for me
is just part of the harness.

00:09:33.120 --> 00:09:35.560 line:95% align:center position:50%
The lore is the lore,
the universe is the universe,

00:09:35.600 --> 00:09:37.880 line:95% align:center position:50%
and the scenario is one
story in this universe.

00:09:39.880 --> 00:09:44.880 line:95% align:center position:50%
How to write, what are the rules,
what are the different steps that

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:49.440 line:95% align:center position:50%
the harness has to follow, etc.

00:09:49.520 --> 00:09:52.600 line:95% align:center position:50%
Once it's done,
then comes the— Inner loop.

00:09:52.760 --> 00:09:55.160 line:95% align:center position:50%
So the inner loop is
an agile writing loop.

00:09:55.560 --> 00:10:01.160 line:95% align:center position:50%
So I am still a human in the loop here,
and it's at chapter level.

00:10:01.280 --> 00:10:04.960 line:95% align:center position:50%
So the writing procedure is
write chapter by chapter.

00:10:05.640 --> 00:10:08.720 line:95% align:center position:50%
In the AI harness, the whole
scenario is already described.

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:12.480 line:95% align:center position:50%
Synopsis, detailed scenario,
very detailed scenario, etc.

00:10:12.760 --> 00:10:14.040 line:95% align:center position:50%
Everything is described, right?

00:10:14.480 --> 00:10:18.880 line:95% align:center position:50%
So now we have to write,
implement the scenario, right?

00:10:18.960 --> 00:10:23.720 line:95% align:center position:50%
So based on the rules from the AI
harness, first contact injection.

00:10:24.080 --> 00:10:29.280 line:95% align:center position:50%
Grab all the MD files from the lore as
code that are relevant to the writing

00:10:29.320 --> 00:10:34.120 line:95% align:center position:50%
of this particular chapter,
then do a first structural draft for me

00:10:34.160 --> 00:10:39.120 line:95% align:center position:50%
to check, and then expenses through
different passes until I say— and that's

00:10:39.160 --> 00:10:43.160 line:95% align:center position:50%
me— say, okay, that's okay,
let's move to the next chapter.

00:10:43.640 --> 00:10:44.260 line:95% align:center position:50%
Right.

00:10:44.920 --> 00:10:48.800 line:95% align:center position:50%
Once I did that with all the different
chapters, so in white you have

00:10:49.360 --> 00:10:52.760 line:95% align:center position:50%
the foundation and the inner loop,
then we go into the author loop.

00:10:53.040 --> 00:10:57.960 line:95% align:center position:50%
The outer loop is about
the book itself, right?

00:10:58.280 --> 00:11:01.520 line:95% align:center position:50%
So what I need to do is to compile
the book, to create the book.

00:11:01.600 --> 00:11:03.320 line:95% align:center position:50%
So for that, I have a compile phase.

00:11:03.600 --> 00:11:08.040 line:95% align:center position:50%
Basically, it's a script using Pandoc
because everything is in Markdown.

00:11:08.440 --> 00:11:11.600 line:95% align:center position:50%
And I have 2 targets for generation.

00:11:11.680 --> 00:11:12.760 line:95% align:center position:50%
The first one is PDF.

00:11:13.240 --> 00:11:16.520 line:95% align:center position:50%
PDF will be used to do the coverback
version of the book, this one.

00:11:17.320 --> 00:11:19.040 line:95% align:center position:50%
And the second one is EPUB.

00:11:19.200 --> 00:11:25.960 line:95% align:center position:50%
That will be the The— how do you call
that— the book for Kindles and the ebook.

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:27.020 line:95% align:center position:50%
Yeah, sorry.

00:11:27.560 --> 00:11:27.960 line:95% align:center position:50%
Right.

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:33.040 line:95% align:center position:50%
So just again, I have my source and then I
compile it and I have different

00:11:33.680 --> 00:11:38.040 line:95% align:center position:50%
instructions to add the COVID and to have
specific formatting

00:11:38.400 --> 00:11:40.080 line:95% align:center position:50%
depending on the target.
Right.

00:11:41.040 --> 00:11:44.720 line:95% align:center position:50%
Once the book is compiled,
then I go through a QA phase.

00:11:44.960 --> 00:11:47.120 line:95% align:center position:50%
And for that, I use LLM as judge.

00:11:47.800 --> 00:11:50.520 line:95% align:center position:50%
All right.
Or as judges, because I used 3.

00:11:50.880 --> 00:11:54.120 line:95% align:center position:50%
So I used Gemini CLI as the lore guardian.

00:11:54.720 --> 00:11:54.960 line:95% align:center position:50%
Okay.

00:11:55.360 --> 00:11:59.720 line:95% align:center position:50%
So checking that everything is coherent,
even if I had my RNS and stuff,

00:11:59.960 --> 00:12:04.520 line:95% align:center position:50%
just like we do with AI SDLC agentic
workflows, put this verification

00:12:04.560 --> 00:12:05.560 line:95% align:center position:50%
part in the loop, right?

00:12:05.840 --> 00:12:08.720 line:95% align:center position:50%
So check that everything is coherent
with what I described

00:12:08.760 --> 00:12:09.880 line:95% align:center position:50%
in the lore and everything.

00:12:12.240 --> 00:12:16.720 line:95% align:center position:50%
The Codex and the GPT models
behind it was the dramatic analyst.

00:12:16.800 --> 00:12:23.120 line:95% align:center position:50%
So it was not about lore, it was about the
way the scenario and the writing is done.

00:12:23.200 --> 00:12:28.760 line:95% align:center position:50%
Is it fulfilling the best
practices of storytelling, right?

00:12:29.720 --> 00:12:31.400 line:95% align:center position:50%
Is there enough suspense?

00:12:31.920 --> 00:12:32.880 line:95% align:center position:50%
How it is written?

00:12:33.480 --> 00:12:35.080 line:95% align:center position:50%
What is the rhythm of the story?

00:12:35.400 --> 00:12:38.880 line:95% align:center position:50%
Even if I did inject that in the beginning
again, but still

00:12:39.480 --> 00:12:42.160 line:95% align:center position:50%
verify that and challenge the book, right?

00:12:42.520 --> 00:12:45.400 line:95% align:center position:50%
And Mistral, yes,
I use it because I'm French, but also

00:12:45.880 --> 00:12:51.400 line:95% align:center position:50%
even if it's not an American model
for the stylistic editor, I wanted to have

00:12:52.200 --> 00:12:57.080 line:95% align:center position:50%
a view on how the style is,
the style of the book, of the writing

00:12:57.600 --> 00:13:00.200 line:95% align:center position:50%
from a model that was not American.

00:13:01.480 --> 00:13:03.400 line:95% align:center position:50%
So, and that many loops.
All right.

00:13:03.480 --> 00:13:06.480 line:95% align:center position:50%
Because yes, I took
into consideration some

00:13:06.600 --> 00:13:10.760 line:95% align:center position:50%
of the recommendations or the remarks or
the reviews from those different models.

00:13:11.040 --> 00:13:13.520 line:95% align:center position:50%
And then up we go and we
go several loops like that.

00:13:13.920 --> 00:13:14.500 line:95% align:center position:50%
Right.

00:13:15.200 --> 00:13:18.400 line:95% align:center position:50%
So there we go.
When it's ready, then the book is ready.

00:13:18.880 --> 00:13:23.080 line:95% align:center position:50%
But you still have to deploy it just
like any software that we will deploy.

00:13:23.760 --> 00:13:27.360 line:95% align:center position:50%
This time we enter a jungle
that's called the Amazon jungle.

00:13:27.960 --> 00:13:29.680 line:95% align:center position:50%
Sorry for the pun, but that's real.

00:13:29.720 --> 00:13:34.200 line:95% align:center position:50%
It's first a jungle because there's a lot
of tools to use to publish on Amazon.

00:13:35.400 --> 00:13:39.080 line:95% align:center position:50%
You can first review both
the paperback and the Kindle versions.

00:13:39.520 --> 00:13:44.120 line:95% align:center position:50%
So for that you use— for the Kindle
version, you use Kindle Previewer to see

00:13:44.400 --> 00:13:47.720 line:95% align:center position:50%
how your EPUB will look like when it will

00:13:47.800 --> 00:13:52.080 line:95% align:center position:50%
be compiled by Amazon and served

00:13:52.200 --> 00:13:54.040 line:95% align:center position:50%
as an ebook on their platform.

00:13:54.440 --> 00:13:58.400 line:95% align:center position:50%
Then you also have to design the covers,
as I mentioned, the blurb,

00:13:58.480 --> 00:14:03.120 line:95% align:center position:50%
the description, so all the metadata
that will appear on Amazon Books.

00:14:04.560 --> 00:14:09.200 line:95% align:center position:50%
Then you also have to define prices,
how much will the book cost,

00:14:09.600 --> 00:14:14.000 line:95% align:center position:50%
marketplace where the book will be sold,
and campaigns if you want

00:14:14.040 --> 00:14:15.120 line:95% align:center position:50%
to do marketing campaigns.

00:14:15.880 --> 00:14:19.800 line:95% align:center position:50%
And then when you've done all that and you
tested everything, then yes,

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:22.680 line:95% align:center position:50%
you can go and publish your book.
It's on Amazon.

00:14:23.120 --> 00:14:24.040 line:95% align:center position:50%
It's there, right?

00:14:24.640 --> 00:14:27.440 line:95% align:center position:50%
So here you have,
and you know Amazon, I guess.

00:14:27.600 --> 00:14:31.240 line:95% align:center position:50%
So you have the 2 versions,
the Kindle and the paperback one, right?

00:14:32.280 --> 00:14:33.560 line:95% align:center position:50%
So this is this one, right?

00:14:36.280 --> 00:14:41.800 line:95% align:center position:50%
The point is that yes, here you have
your workflow, but there's the last part.

00:14:42.120 --> 00:14:43.920 line:95% align:center position:50%
We do observability
when we design systems.

00:14:44.000 --> 00:14:45.540 line:95% align:center position:50%
As an architect, I'd like to know
what's going on in my system.

00:14:47.280 --> 00:14:50.720 line:95% align:center position:50%
So I want to know what's going on about
my book because basically if I wrote

00:14:50.760 --> 00:14:54.240 line:95% align:center position:50%
a book to tell a story,
maybe I want people to read the story

00:14:54.760 --> 00:14:56.080 line:95% align:center position:50%
or give me feedback on that.

00:14:56.400 --> 00:14:58.120 line:95% align:center position:50%
So the last part is monitoring, right?

00:14:58.200 --> 00:15:01.720 line:95% align:center position:50%
For that you have Amazon Author Central,
which is yet another tool.

00:15:02.920 --> 00:15:04.680 line:95% align:center position:50%
But then you discover the real jungle.

00:15:04.960 --> 00:15:08.480 line:95% align:center position:50%
And the real jungle is not the jungle
of tools, it's the jungle of books.

00:15:08.880 --> 00:15:13.200 line:95% align:center position:50%
Because Amazon makes it so easy to publish
books and AI so easy to write them

00:15:13.600 --> 00:15:16.160 line:95% align:center position:50%
that every day you have hundreds
of new books on the platform.

00:15:16.680 --> 00:15:18.480 line:95% align:center position:50%
So how to exist?
How to be visible?

00:15:19.680 --> 00:15:23.720 line:95% align:center position:50%
Well, you can tell your friends,
your colleagues, your cats, your dogs,

00:15:24.040 --> 00:15:28.960 line:95% align:center position:50%
you give talks in conferences,
wink, try to be visible.

00:15:30.320 --> 00:15:34.960 line:95% align:center position:50%
The point is that many years ago I had
to choose in my studies between

00:15:35.000 --> 00:15:36.640 line:95% align:center position:50%
engineering and business.
And guess what?

00:15:36.680 --> 00:15:38.040 line:95% align:center position:50%
I didn't choose the last one.

00:15:38.520 --> 00:15:41.320 line:95% align:center position:50%
I prefer designing systems,
not selling them.

00:15:43.080 --> 00:15:45.080 line:95% align:center position:50%
And that's why I discovered the hard way
that there's a part

00:15:45.120 --> 00:15:46.620 line:95% align:center position:50%
missing in my workflow.
It's the advertising.

00:15:48.160 --> 00:15:49.360 line:95% align:center position:50%
Advertisement part, right?

00:15:49.520 --> 00:15:50.920 line:95% align:center position:50%
How to make your book visible.

00:15:51.920 --> 00:15:55.560 line:95% align:center position:50%
And to do that,
you might need some agency there.

00:15:55.800 --> 00:16:00.320 line:95% align:center position:50%
So maybe it's a human one,
so people who are already— that's their

00:16:00.360 --> 00:16:03.920 line:95% align:center position:50%
job and they know how to promote your book
and make it known on different platforms,

00:16:03.960 --> 00:16:05.720 line:95% align:center position:50%
different forums, communities, and stuff.

00:16:06.280 --> 00:16:08.240 line:95% align:center position:50%
Or maybe you could design your own agent.

00:16:08.280 --> 00:16:14.320 line:95% align:center position:50%
So I'm thinking about maybe I should use
CoWork or OpenClaw to flood the internet

00:16:14.400 --> 00:16:19.160 line:95% align:center position:50%
with things on my But that's not
what I was interested in, really.

00:16:19.400 --> 00:16:21.680 line:95% align:center position:50%
And actually, that's a loop also, right?

00:16:22.440 --> 00:16:27.560 line:95% align:center position:50%
Instead of that, I said, no, I want to
concentrate and focus on the book itself.

00:16:27.960 --> 00:16:33.640 line:95% align:center position:50%
And yet I used the "mise en abyme" name,
which is a very, very posh and

00:16:34.400 --> 00:16:36.600 line:95% align:center position:50%
literary way to say fractal, right?

00:16:37.040 --> 00:16:40.560 line:95% align:center position:50%
So in my book,
my pen name, as I said, is Raphiki.

00:16:40.880 --> 00:16:43.600 line:95% align:center position:50%
But Raphiki is also
a character in the universe.

00:16:43.960 --> 00:16:46.280 line:95% align:center position:50%
Right?
So it's a kind of inception stuff.

00:16:48.280 --> 00:16:50.680 line:95% align:center position:50%
He's the author of the book's interludes,
because you have some

00:16:50.720 --> 00:16:52.960 line:95% align:center position:50%
interludes in the book.

00:16:53.080 --> 00:16:55.800 line:95% align:center position:50%
He's the author of the book itself,
but in the universe,

00:16:55.960 --> 00:16:57.600 line:95% align:center position:50%
he's the author of the interludes.

00:16:57.640 --> 00:17:00.880 line:95% align:center position:50%
And it's a kind of alter ego of myself,

00:17:00.960 --> 00:17:05.280 line:95% align:center position:50%
a dystopian self in 2036.
Sorry.

00:17:06.040 --> 00:17:07.080 line:95% align:center position:50%
Well, why I did that?

00:17:07.280 --> 00:17:08.800 line:95% align:center position:50%
Because I found it cool.

00:17:08.840 --> 00:17:10.920 line:95% align:center position:50%
I wanted to have this
special feature in my book.

00:17:11.320 --> 00:17:13.680 line:95% align:center position:50%
And it's also the dream of every game
master to get to play

00:17:15.560 --> 00:17:18.520 line:95% align:center position:50%
real character, not only
the non-personal characters, you know.

00:17:18.800 --> 00:17:21.480 line:95% align:center position:50%
So I have my own characters
in the story, I'm happy, right?

00:17:22.600 --> 00:17:26.520 line:95% align:center position:50%
So here we are, the book is ready, it's
here, you have the QR code you can scan.

00:17:27.120 --> 00:17:29.800 line:95% align:center position:50%
But then, and actually that was
from the early beginning,

00:17:29.920 --> 00:17:31.480 line:95% align:center position:50%
I decided to go further than that.

00:17:31.920 --> 00:17:35.440 line:95% align:center position:50%
Because as I said,
the book is only one output of my lore.

00:17:36.040 --> 00:17:40.320 line:95% align:center position:50%
So that leads us to chapter 2,
transmedia storytelling.

00:17:40.920 --> 00:17:43.320 line:95% align:center position:50%
Because Laura Scott,
as I said, is a foundation.

00:17:43.400 --> 00:17:45.040 line:95% align:center position:50%
That's where I spend most of my time,
that's what I like to do,

00:17:45.080 --> 00:17:47.560 line:95% align:center position:50%
that's what I like to design.
That's what you're good at.

00:17:47.600 --> 00:17:48.800 line:95% align:center position:50%
And create, right?

00:17:49.080 --> 00:17:51.120 line:95% align:center position:50%
And the book was just one output of that.

00:17:51.560 --> 00:17:55.040 line:95% align:center position:50%
You can have some expansion or other
outputs based on the same lore.

00:17:55.760 --> 00:17:58.400 line:95% align:center position:50%
So I decided to create
an alternate reality game.

00:17:58.560 --> 00:18:00.720 line:95% align:center position:50%
Do you know what it is,
alternate reality game?

00:18:01.320 --> 00:18:01.920 line:95% align:center position:50%
Just a game.

00:18:02.480 --> 00:18:06.120 line:95% align:center position:50%
Actually, it's the form of a website,
and we will deep dive into that,

00:18:06.440 --> 00:18:10.560 line:95% align:center position:50%
where readers can access some online
archive and have more content

00:18:10.760 --> 00:18:13.000 line:95% align:center position:50%
about the story, about the lore.

00:18:14.200 --> 00:18:16.640 line:95% align:center position:50%
I tried also, I started
visual rendering the book.

00:18:16.680 --> 00:18:19.400 line:95% align:center position:50%
So I have a graphic graphic
novel version of the book.

00:18:19.800 --> 00:18:23.920 line:95% align:center position:50%
And since the start,
it has always been a series in my mind.

00:18:23.960 --> 00:18:26.800 line:95% align:center position:50%
So I already have part 2 and part 3.

00:18:27.920 --> 00:18:28.160 line:95% align:center position:50%
Right.

00:18:28.400 --> 00:18:31.960 line:95% align:center position:50%
Because basically, the book,
from the reader's point of view,

00:18:32.280 --> 00:18:34.800 line:95% align:center position:50%
is only the gateway to this lore,
to this universe.

00:18:35.120 --> 00:18:40.840 line:95% align:center position:50%
And then when you enter it— and that's
the case with this book— like on page 175,

00:18:43.800 --> 00:18:50.160 line:95% align:center position:50%
after a very hardcore chapter, very
emotionally intense chapter, this QR code.

00:18:50.560 --> 00:18:55.440 line:95% align:center position:50%
This one you won't be able to scan because
it's for the people who bought

00:18:55.480 --> 00:18:56.960 line:95% align:center position:50%
the book, you understand why.

00:18:57.000 --> 00:19:00.080 line:95% align:center position:50%
And there is this sentence,
scan if you are still human.

00:19:01.080 --> 00:19:07.120 line:95% align:center position:50%
And then when the reader is doing that,
then slightly he's shifted from the book

00:19:07.600 --> 00:19:13.600 line:95% align:center position:50%
to the ARG, to the website that I created,
which is in-universe.

00:19:13.720 --> 00:19:17.000 line:95% align:center position:50%
So you see, or you don't see,
but the copyright is 2036.

00:19:17.240 --> 00:19:18.840 line:95% align:center position:50%
Right.

00:19:19.240 --> 00:19:21.440 line:95% align:center position:50%
So that's alternate
reality game, what it is.

00:19:22.360 --> 00:19:23.000 line:95% align:center position:50%
It's a portal.

00:19:23.320 --> 00:19:26.440 line:95% align:center position:50%
You have riddles and games
that you have to solve.

00:19:26.800 --> 00:19:30.280 line:95% align:center position:50%
And as you solve the riddles,
you enter first the portal, and then you

00:19:30.320 --> 00:19:32.280 line:95% align:center position:50%
go through different clearance levels.

00:19:32.640 --> 00:19:38.000 line:95% align:center position:50%
And as long as you unlock those clearance
levels, you have access to extra content,

00:19:38.360 --> 00:19:43.480 line:95% align:center position:50%
extra lore, extra unpublished chapters,
or maybe preview of the

00:19:44.360 --> 00:19:45.680 line:95% align:center position:50%
next books in the series.

00:19:46.280 --> 00:19:50.680 line:95% align:center position:50%
I might inject into that the graphic
novel version, that kind of stuff, right?

00:19:51.160 --> 00:19:54.720 line:95% align:center position:50%
The idea is to embark people
in my universe, in the lore, right?

00:19:55.280 --> 00:20:00.520 line:95% align:center position:50%
And I also made my own monitoring
console just to check how many

00:20:00.560 --> 00:20:01.920 line:95% align:center position:50%
people did scan from the book.

00:20:02.000 --> 00:20:04.040 line:95% align:center position:50%
That's why it can only be scanned there.

00:20:05.200 --> 00:20:07.560 line:95% align:center position:50%
What are the— where are
the people in different levels?

00:20:08.960 --> 00:20:13.800 line:95% align:center position:50%
And I can activate or deactivate the
clearance for level as I see fit, right?

00:20:14.560 --> 00:20:19.240 line:95% align:center position:50%
So to create the application,
the ARG, there's a workflow.

00:20:19.280 --> 00:20:20.540 line:95% align:center position:50%
This one is more classic.

00:20:20.800 --> 00:20:22.080 line:95% align:center position:50%
I mean, it's software, right?

00:20:22.440 --> 00:20:26.840 line:95% align:center position:50%
It's just the part Laura Scott is always
there because it's what unifies

00:20:26.880 --> 00:20:28.160 line:95% align:center position:50%
the whole universe, right?

00:20:28.560 --> 00:20:30.400 line:95% align:center position:50%
And then yes, I have my AI harness.

00:20:30.800 --> 00:20:35.800 line:95% align:center position:50%
I did some kind of speculative development
with architecture, meaning what is the ARG

00:20:35.960 --> 00:20:40.160 line:95% align:center position:50%
about, the why, so what is the strategy,
what do I want to achieve with that.

00:20:41.080 --> 00:20:47.320 line:95% align:center position:50%
The what is the UX/UI, what is it,
how it will be constructed.

00:20:47.600 --> 00:20:51.320 line:95% align:center position:50%
And the how, sorry, is the architecture
part and the tech part, right?

00:20:51.760 --> 00:20:56.280 line:95% align:center position:50%
Then yes, building, it's a Dockerized
application, TypeScript, basic stuff.

00:20:56.600 --> 00:20:59.720 line:95% align:center position:50%
And then I have my transmedia
storytelling loop.

00:21:01.000 --> 00:21:05.560 line:95% align:center position:50%
Each time I add new content on the portal,
then it's regenerated

00:21:05.640 --> 00:21:06.960 line:95% align:center position:50%
and redeployed, right?

00:21:07.440 --> 00:21:14.283 line:95% align:center position:50%
So the URL, the QR code here, if you
scan it or if you go on the-human-protocol.com,

00:21:14.483 --> 00:21:16.320 line:95% align:center position:50%
then you access this ARG.

00:21:16.720 --> 00:21:18.680 line:95% align:center position:50%
And then you can start trying to solve.

00:21:19.200 --> 00:21:23.560 line:95% align:center position:50%
You might need the book to solve because
the clues of most of the riddles

00:21:23.600 --> 00:21:28.120 line:95% align:center position:50%
are hidden in the book.
So there's kind of a mystery there, right?

00:21:29.040 --> 00:21:30.720 line:95% align:center position:50%
Okay, so that was the first expansion.

00:21:31.080 --> 00:21:34.600 line:95% align:center position:50%
The second one I tried is a novel
adaptation So how

00:21:34.680 --> 00:21:36.760 line:95% align:center position:50%
to visually render the story.

00:21:38.120 --> 00:21:41.560 line:95% align:center position:50%
So here are some examples of the outcome.

00:21:41.640 --> 00:21:46.440 line:95% align:center position:50%
It's a work in progress still,
but still it's the same idea.

00:21:46.760 --> 00:21:50.280 line:95% align:center position:50%
It's grounded in the lore-as-code
and in the book, in the actual

00:21:50.360 --> 00:21:51.520 line:95% align:center position:50%
chapters of the book, right?

00:21:51.920 --> 00:21:56.400 line:95% align:center position:50%
So the story in the cartoon is the same as
in the book because it's

00:21:56.480 --> 00:21:57.600 line:95% align:center position:50%
the same source, right?

00:21:58.400 --> 00:22:04.360 line:95% align:center position:50%
But there's more human labor here because
I decided that I wanted to position myself

00:22:04.720 --> 00:22:08.400 line:95% align:center position:50%
the bubbles and the text to have
more control on the output.

00:22:08.880 --> 00:22:10.440 line:95% align:center position:50%
So it's a bit less automated.

00:22:10.480 --> 00:22:12.440 line:95% align:center position:50%
It's not finished yet,
so it's taking time.

00:22:13.360 --> 00:22:16.080 line:95% align:center position:50%
But yeah,
the results are kind of interesting

00:22:16.280 --> 00:22:19.280 line:95% align:center position:50%
because I had to anchor everything
in visual references

00:22:20.280 --> 00:22:24.120 line:95% align:center position:50%
to make sure that Elara,
who is the main character of the story,

00:22:24.440 --> 00:22:28.440 line:95% align:center position:50%
has the same face, has the same gears,
the universe is coherent.

00:22:30.840 --> 00:22:32.760 line:95% align:center position:50%
And last part is lore expansion.

00:22:32.960 --> 00:22:36.400 line:95% align:center position:50%
So of course now I'm working
on translating the book in French.

00:22:36.960 --> 00:22:40.160 line:95% align:center position:50%
And here I have an issue now because
French is my native language.

